1. Scope and definitions

This is a custom source-available license. It restricts commercial exploitation
and redistribution and is not an OSI Open Source license. The source is publicly
available for transparency, personal use, review, and community contribution.

"Licensor" means Nemoforge (DINH DUC LOC). "Software" means the Junction Manager
source code and associated documentation made available under this license,
starting with V1.0.0. "You" means the individual or organization exercising rights
under this license. A "modified version" includes a changed, adapted, translated,
repackaged, or rebranded copy, or a work incorporating a substantial portion of
the Software. A "distribution" includes providing source, scripts, binaries,
archives, installers, or access to copies to others.

This license grants only rights the Licensor is entitled to grant. Separately
licensed third-party materials remain subject to their own terms and notices;
this license does not relicense them. Windows, PowerShell, .NET, and other system
components are not licensed by this document merely because the Software uses
them. Rights not expressly granted are reserved, subject to section 11.

2. Free personal, internal, educational, and review use

Subject to this license, the Licensor grants you a worldwide, non-exclusive,
royalty-free copyright license to:

(a) Download, copy, install, run, and use the Software for personal purposes on
    any number of computers you own or are authorized to administer.
(b) Use and copy the Software within an organization, including a for-profit
    business, to manage its own computers. Employees and authorized contractors
    may use it on that organization's behalf for these internal purposes.
(c) Modify, build, and run private copies for your personal use or your
    organization's internal use, and share those copies only with personnel
    acting for that organization for those purposes.
(d) Read and study the source, learn from it, conduct education, research and
    authorized security review, write reviews or tutorials, and report bugs or
    vulnerabilities. Reasonable source quotations permitted by applicable
    copyright law remain permitted.
(e) Prepare and submit community contributions as described in section 3.

Ordinary internal business use is allowed without payment to the Licensor.
An IT administrator may use the Software at work. A business earning revenue,
or paying employees or contractors for internal administration, does not by
itself make that internal use prohibited commercial exploitation. This exception
does not permit selling or offering the Software to customers as a product or
monetized service. Section 5 defines the commercial activities requiring consent.

3. Contribution forks and patches

You may fork the official repository on GitHub, modify the fork to prepare a
contribution, submit pull requests upstream, and share patches or diffs with the
official project. A public contribution fork is an express exception to the
modified-redistribution restriction in section 4, provided that it:

(a) Is clearly identified as a contribution fork based on Junction Manager;
(b) Retains the copyright, attribution, and LICENSE notices;
(c) Is not promoted or supplied as a competing or replacement product; and
(d) Does not publish standalone public packages or releases for general use.

Sharing source changes for upstream review does not authorize a separately
marketed fork. Section 11 preserves rights granted independently by GitHub.
Deliberately submitted contributions are subject to section 8.

4. Redistribution

You may freely share links to the official repository and its official release
pages. Linking does not grant additional rights in the Software.

You may mirror an unmodified official release without prior written permission
only if all of the following conditions are met:

(a) The original release files remain unchanged, without repackaging, added
    installers, bundled software, renaming as another product, or altered code;
(b) Access and download are free, without paid licensing, paid access, resale,
    or other monetized redistribution as described in section 5;
(c) All copyright and author notices are retained and the complete LICENSE
    accompanies the copy; it may accompany an unchanged release archive;
(d) The mirror identifies the original version and clearly states:
    "Unofficial mirror of an unmodified official Junction Manager release";
(e) A prominent link points to the official repository and original release
    page, with the official download recommended as the primary source; and
(f) The mirror does not claim to be an official publisher or endorsed service,
    impose replacement license terms, or present the Software as its own product.

Private/internal sharing under section 2 and contribution forks under section 3
are also allowed. Apart from these express permissions and section 11, public
redistribution of modified versions, independent builds, or forks requires the
Licensor's prior written permission, even when offered free of charge. Other
redistribution not expressly permitted here also requires written permission.

You may not take the Software or a substantial portion of it, rename or rebrand
it, and publish it as your own or a competing product without prior written
permission. An allowed, accurately labeled mirror is not a competing product.
Private modifications need no redistribution permission while kept within the
personal/internal scope of section 2.

5. Commercial exploitation requiring written permission

Without the Licensor's prior written permission covering the specific activity,
you may not use the Software or a substantial portion of it, including a modified
version, for any of the following:

(a) Selling, reselling, paid licensing, or charging for downloads or access;
(b) Incorporating it into a commercial software product or commercial service
    offered to customers, or using it as the foundation of a paid product;
(c) Providing SaaS, hosted access, or another monetized service whose primary
    functionality or value is supplied by the Software;
(d) Bundling it with a commercial software package or product, or supplying it
    through paid OEM distribution or preinstallation on products sold to others;
(e) Monetized redistribution, including revenue specifically tied to supplying
    copies or access, regardless of whether the copy is advertised as free; or
(f) Selling support, licenses, subscriptions, or access based on a fork or
    marketing a modified version as a commercial product.

The personal and internal organizational uses expressly permitted by section 2
are excluded from these restrictions. Authorized security research, review,
teaching, or permitted technical quotation is not prohibited solely because the
researcher, reviewer, teacher, or writer receives compensation; this does not
permit selling copies, access, or a fork-based support service.

6. Malicious use and harmful modifications

You may not use, modify, or distribute the Software or its derivatives with
malicious intent to deploy malware, spyware, ransomware, credential theft,
unauthorized persistence, destructive payloads, or backdoors; to bypass security
controls to cause harm or obtain unauthorized access; or to impersonate an
official update or release to deceive users.

This restriction targets harmful conduct. It does not prohibit lawful,
authorized security research, controlled testing on systems you own or have
permission to test, vulnerability analysis, or good-faith reporting. Research
does not independently authorize public distribution of a modified build;
section 4 still applies, subject to section 11.

